## Overview
In this PR we fix the issue of getting errors while sending direct debit notifications.

## Before
Direct debit notification fails 
![asasasasas](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/85277674/202393284-c3ea2696-9f1c-41ce-aa6f-6992d33ee9c0.gif)


## After
Direct debit notifications succeed
![fddfdf](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/85277674/202392645-8c462406-9e7c-4fa3-b2c9-992045022862.gif)


## Technical Details
Sending direct debit notifications fails on CiviCRM version >= 5.51.0 because we check the contact `preferred_mail_format` field to determine if the mail format should be text, HTML or both, but the `preference_mail_format` is no longer supported see the discussion here https://lab.civicrm.org/dev/core/-/issues/2866, so when this conditional block runs both the `$tokenText` and `$tokenHtml` variables are NULL, and NULL messages cannot be sent resulting in an error.

```php
      if ($values['preferred_mail_format'] == 'Text' || $values['preferred_mail_format'] == 'Both') {
        $tokenText = CRM_Utils_Token::replaceContactTokens($text, $values, FALSE, $messageToken, FALSE, $escapeSmarty);
        $tokenText = CRM_Utils_Token::replaceHookTokens($tokenText, $values, $categories, FALSE, $escapeSmarty);
      }
      else {
        $tokenText = NULL;
      }

      if ($values['preferred_mail_format'] == 'HTML' || $values['preferred_mail_format'] == 'Both') {
        $tokenHtml = CRM_Utils_Token::replaceContactTokens($html, $values, TRUE, $messageToken, FALSE, $escapeSmarty);
        $tokenHtml = CRM_Utils_Token::replaceHookTokens($tokenHtml, $values, $categories, TRUE, $escapeSmarty);
      }
      else {
        $tokenHtml = NULL;
      }
```

We resolved this error by removing the `if` blocks and sending the text and HTML messages together and letting the user mail client handle it as necessary as mentioned [here](https://lab.civicrm.org/dev/core/-/issues/2866), we also used the opportunity to clean up the `sendDirectDebitEmail` function, by removing legacy codes and using the CiviCRM core `renderTemplate` function to render the message template.

